    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Build succeeds and all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds membership level 4, gated on tenure over 365 days, satisfying the spec: a brand-new owner (registration date defaults to today \u2192 zero tenure) can never exceed level 3.\n\n**What I changed** \u2014 one method in one file (`MembershipLevels.levelOf`):\n- The existing email + `namesakeCount == 0` factors still combine and cap at 3 (`Math.min(level, 3)`).\n- A new branch bumps to 4 only when `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(registrationDate, now) > 365`.\n\n**Why this shape** \u2014 the cost model's dominant term is `WMC_other` (the summed complexity of the *other* methods in the edited method's class). `MembershipLevels` contains only a private constructor besides `levelOf`, so `WMC_other \u2248 1`. Extracting a tenure helper would have created a second changed function whose `WMC_other` would then include `levelOf`'s complexity \u2014 multiplying the cost. Keeping the addition inline in the already-simple method, touching a single file, keeps structural impact minimal.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` (new owner with email, no namesake, 3-member household \u2192 level 3) passes, and the full suite is green.",
